at source. Codex then applies the stricter result from managed requirements and user configuration.&quot;]}],[0,{&quot;key&quot;:[0,&quot;browser_use.default_origin_policy.access&quot;],&quot;type&quot;:[0,&quot;allow | deny&quot;],&quot;description&quot;:[0,&quot;Use `deny` to block Browser Use on origins that use the fallback. A denied origin also blocks uploads, downloads, full browser debugging access, and automatic review there. `allow` only lets normal approval and policy checks continue.&quot;]}],[0,{&quot;key&quot;:[0,&quot;browser_use.default_origin_policy.downloads&quot;],&quot;type&quot;:[0,&quot;allow | deny&quot;],&quot;description&quot;:[0,&quot;Use `deny` to block Browser Use downloads on origins that use the fallback. `allow` only lets normal approval and policy checks continue.&quot;]}],[0,{&quot;key&quot;:[0,&quot;browser_use.default_origin_policy.uploads&quot;],&quot;type&quot;:[0,&quot;allow | deny&quot;],&quot;description&quot;:[0,&quot;Use `deny` to block Browser Use uploads on origins that use the fallback. `allow` only lets normal approval and policy checks continue.&quot;]}],[0,{&quot;key&quot;:[0,&quot;browser_use.default_origin_policy.full_cdp_access&quot;],&quot;type&quot;:[0,&quot;allow | deny&quot;],&quot;description&quot;:[0,&quot;Use `deny` to block full Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP) access on origins that use the fallback. `allow` only lets normal opt-in and approval checks continue.&quot;]}],[0,{&quot;key&quot;:[0,&quot;browser_use.default_origin_policy.auto_review&quot;],&quot;type&quot;:[0,&quot;allow | deny&quot;],&quot;description&quot;:[0,&quot;Use `deny` to skip automatic review on origins that use the fallback and ask the user for approval instead. `allow` leaves automatic review available when other settings allow it.&quot;]}],[0,{&quot;key&quot;:[0,&quot;browser_use.default_origin_policy.persistent_approval&quot;],&quot;type&quot;:[0,&quot;boolean&quot;],&quot;description&quot;:[0,&quot;Set to `false` to prevent Browser Us