p app&#39;s built-in browser into site tools (WebMCP). Setting it to <code>false</code> or omitting it leaves normal feature availability checks in place; <code>false</code> does not enforce a block. User preferences and site permissions still apply.</div></div></div><div class="border-b border-default p-4 last:border-b-0 bg-surface-secondary"><div class="mb-2"><div class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold text-secondary">Key</div><code class="text-sm font-mono text-default bg-transparent!">browser_use.default_origin_policy</code></div><div class="mb-2"><div class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold text-secondary">Type / Values</div><code class="whitespace-pre-wrap text-sm font-mono text-default bg-transparent!">table</code></div><div><div class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold text-secondary">Details</div><div class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-default [&amp;_a]:font-medium [&amp;_a]:underline [&amp;_a]:underline-offset-2 [&amp;_a]:text-link-color hover:[&amp;_a]:text-link-color-hover [&amp;_code]:rounded-sm [&amp;_code]:bg-surface-secondary [&amp;_code]:px-1 [&amp;_code]:py-0.5 [&amp;_code]:font-mono [&amp;_code]:text-[0.95em]">Fallback for each Browser Use setting when no matching entry under <code>browser_use.origins</code> defines it. A matching origin rule replaces the fallback for that source. Codex then applies the stricter result from managed requirements and user configuration.</div></div></div><div class="border-b border-default p-4 last:border-b-0 bg-surface"><div class="mb-2"><div class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold text-secondary">Key</div><code class="text-sm font-mono text-default bg-transparent!">browser_use.default_origin_policy.access</code></div><div class="mb-2"><div class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold text-secondary">Type / Values</div><code class="whitespace-pre-wrap text-sm font-mono text-default bg-transparent!">allow | deny</code></div><div><div class="mb-1 text-xs font-semibold text-secondary">Details</div><div class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-default [&amp;